{"title":"Methods & Data","markdown":{"yaml":{"page-layout":"full","toc":false},"headingText":"Methods & Data","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n<style>\n.section-hero,\n.methods-section {\n  position: relative;\n  left: 50%;\n  transform: translateX(-50%);\n  width: min(1200px, 92vw);\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  margin: 0;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n.section-hero {\n  padding: 2.6rem 2rem 1.6rem 2rem;\n}\n\n.methods-section {\n  padding: 0.8rem 2rem 2.8rem 2rem;\n}\n\n.section-hero h1,\n.methods-section h2 {\n  width: 100%;\n  margin-left: auto;\n  margin-right: auto;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n.section-hero p,\n.methods-section > p {\n  max-width: 920px;\n  margin-left: auto;\n  margin-right: auto;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------\n   Data source cards\n--------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n.data-grid {\n  width: min(1050px, 92vw);\n  margin: 1.6rem auto 0 auto;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);\n  gap: 16px;\n}\n\n.data-card {\n  background: #FAF7F0;\n  border: 1px solid #E3D6B8;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 1.25rem 1.3rem;\n  text-align: left;\n  box-shadow: 0 5px 14px rgba(23, 77, 56, 0.06);\n}\n\n.data-card h3 {\n  margin-top: 0;\n  margin-bottom: 0.6rem;\n  color: #174D38;\n  font-size: 1.08rem;\n}\n\n.data-card p {\n  margin: 0;\n  line-height: 1.65;\n  color: #2B2B2B;\n}\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------\n   Workflow\n--------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n.workflow {\n  width: min(1080px, 94vw);\n  margin: 2rem auto 0 auto;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns:\n    1fr auto\n    1fr auto\n    1fr auto\n    1fr auto\n    1fr auto\n    1fr;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 10px;\n}\n\n.workflow-step {\n  background: #FAF7F0;\n  border: 1px solid #D9C89F;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 1rem 0.75rem;\n  min-height: 125px;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  justify-content: center;\n  box-shadow: 0 5px 14px rgba(23, 77, 56, 0.06);\n}\n\n.workflow-number {\n  font-size: 1.35rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: #C5A45A;\n  margin-bottom: 0.35rem;\n}\n\n.workflow-title {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: #174D38;\n  margin-bottom: 0.35rem;\n  font-size: 0.98rem;\n}\n\n.workflow-text {\n  font-size: 0.82rem;\n  line-height: 1.4;\n  color: #65766D;\n}\n\n.workflow-arrow {\n  font-size: 1.5rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: #C5A45A;\n}\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------\n   Priority weights\n--------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n.weight-grid {\n  width: min(900px, 90vw);\n  margin: 1.5rem auto 0 auto;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);\n  gap: 14px;\n}\n\n.weight-card {\n  background: #FAF7F0;\n  border: 1px solid #E3D6B8;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 1.15rem 0.85rem;\n  box-shadow: 0 5px 14px rgba(23, 77, 56, 0.06);\n}\n\n.weight-card .weight {\n  display: block;\n  font-size: 1.5rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: #174D38;\n  margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n}\n\n.weight-card .label {\n  display: block;\n  color: #2B2B2B;\n  line-height: 1.4;\n}\n\n/* Smaller supporting chart */\n\n.chart-wrap {\n  width: min(700px, 72vw);\n  margin: 1.8rem auto 0 auto;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n.chart-wrap img {\n  display: block;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: auto;\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(23, 77, 56, 0.07);\n}\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------\n   Notes\n--------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n.method-note {\n  max-width: 920px;\n  margin: 1.5rem auto 0 auto;\n  padding: 1rem 1.25rem;\n  background: #FAF7F0;\n  border-left: 4px solid #C5A45A;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  text-align: left;\n  color: #2B2B2B;\n  line-height: 1.7;\n}\n\n.limitations-grid {\n  width: min(1000px, 92vw);\n  margin: 1.5rem auto 0 auto;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);\n  gap: 14px;\n}\n\n.limitation-card {\n  background: #FAF7F0;\n  border: 1px solid #E3D6B8;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  padding: 1rem 1.1rem;\n  text-align: left;\n}\n\n.limitation-card strong {\n  color: #174D38;\n}\n\n.limitation-card p {\n  margin: 0;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------\n   Responsive\n--------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n@media (max-width: 1000px) {\n  .workflow {\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n  }\n\n  .workflow-arrow {\n    transform: rotate(90deg);\n  }\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 800px) {\n  .data-grid,\n  .limitations-grid {\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n  }\n\n  .weight-grid {\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);\n  }\n\n  .chart-wrap {\n    width: min(760px, 92vw);\n  }\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n  .weight-grid {\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n  }\n}\n</style>\n\n::: {.section-hero}\n\n\nCooling Riyadh integrates satellite imagery, population estimates, building footprints, and spatial machine learning within a common **500 m analysis grid**.\n\nThe workflow preserves the spatial meaning of each dataset while allowing multiple urban indicators to be compared consistently across Riyadh.\n\n:::\n\n::: {.methods-section}\n\n## Data Sources\n\n<div class=\"data-grid\">\n\n<div class=\"data-card\">\n\n### Landsat Collection 2 Level-2\n\nUsed to derive **land surface temperature (LST)** and **NDVI**.\n\nSurface reflectance and surface temperature products were processed with cloud and cloud-shadow masking before the Riyadh mosaics were created.\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"data-card\">\n\n### WorldPop 2026\n\nUsed to estimate the spatial distribution of residents across Riyadh.\n\nPopulation values were summarized into the 500 m analysis grid to provide an estimated population for each cell.\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"data-card\">\n\n### Microsoft Building Footprints\n\nUsed to characterize the built environment.\n\nBuilding polygons were clipped to Riyadh and summarized using building count, total building footprint area, and building coverage percentage.\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"data-card\">\n\n### Riyadh Urban Boundary\n\nThe study area was defined using the Riyadh urban boundary extracted from the **Copernicus Global Human Settlement Layer Urban Centre Database**.\n\nThis boundary was used consistently for clipping, raster processing, and final visualization.\n\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n:::\n\n::: {.methods-section}\n\n## Analysis Workflow\n\n<div class=\"workflow\">\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">01</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">Prepare Data</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nClip, clean, and project the source datasets.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-arrow\">→</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">02</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">500 m Grid</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nCreate a common spatial unit across Riyadh.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-arrow\">→</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">03</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">Urban Indicators</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nCalculate LST, NDVI, population, and building metrics.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-arrow\">→</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">04</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">K-Means</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nIdentify recurring urban profiles using unsupervised machine learning.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-arrow\">→</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">05</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">Priority Score</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nCombine normalized indicators into a spatial screening score.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-arrow\">→</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">06</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">AI-Assisted Interpretation</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nCompare urban clusters with High and Very High priority areas.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n:::\n\n::: {.methods-section}\n\n## Priority Score\n\nThe final greening priority score combines four normalized indicators.\n\n<div class=\"weight-grid\">\n\n<div class=\"weight-card\">\n<span class=\"weight\">35%</span>\n<span class=\"label\">Land Surface Temperature</span>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"weight-card\">\n<span class=\"weight\">30%</span>\n<span class=\"label\">Low Vegetation</span>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"weight-card\">\n<span class=\"weight\">25%</span>\n<span class=\"label\">Population Exposure</span>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"weight-card\">\n<span class=\"weight\">10%</span>\n<span class=\"label\">Building Coverage</span>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"chart-wrap\">\n\n![](assets/images/maps/Riyadh_Priority_Weights_Chart.png)\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"method-note\">\n\nThese weights are **analyst-defined** and reflect the project's research question. They are not statistically estimated model coefficients and should be interpreted as a transparent spatial screening framework.\n\n</div>\n\n:::\n\n::: {.methods-section}\n\n## Machine Learning & AI\n\nK-Means clustering was applied to four standardized variables:\n\n**Land Surface Temperature · NDVI · Population · Building Coverage**\n\nThe algorithm grouped spatial cells according to similarity without using predefined labels.\n\nThe resulting urban profiles were then compared with High and Very High greening-priority cells to create the **AI-assisted priority interpretation**.\n\n<div class=\"method-note\">\n\nThe machine-learning analysis supports interpretation of recurring urban conditions. It does **not** generate or replace the weighted greening priority score.\n\n</div>\n\n:::\n\n::: {.methods-section}\n\n## Important Limitations\n\n<div class=\"limitations-grid\">\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Land Surface Temperature</strong><br>\nLST represents satellite-derived surface temperature rather than direct air temperature.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Vegetation</strong><br>\nNDVI indicates vegetation presence but does not distinguish individual trees from grass, shrubs, or other vegetation.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Population</strong><br>\nWorldPop provides modeled population estimates rather than direct census counts for every grid cell.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Buildings</strong><br>\nBuilding footprints describe mapped building geometry but do not directly represent height, occupancy, material, or land use.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Priority Weights</strong><br>\nThe weighting scheme reflects the analytical objectives of this project and is not statistically optimized.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Intervention Readiness</strong><br>\nPriority areas identify locations for further assessment rather than direct planting recommendations.</p>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"method-note\">\n\nLocal land ownership, utilities, road geometry, water availability, existing projects, and planning constraints should be assessed before implementing any greening intervention.\n\n</div>\n\n:::","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n<style>\n.section-hero,\n.methods-section {\n  position: relative;\n  left: 50%;\n  transform: translateX(-50%);\n  width: min(1200px, 92vw);\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  margin: 0;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n.section-hero {\n  padding: 2.6rem 2rem 1.6rem 2rem;\n}\n\n.methods-section {\n  padding: 0.8rem 2rem 2.8rem 2rem;\n}\n\n.section-hero h1,\n.methods-section h2 {\n  width: 100%;\n  margin-left: auto;\n  margin-right: auto;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n.section-hero p,\n.methods-section > p {\n  max-width: 920px;\n  margin-left: auto;\n  margin-right: auto;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------\n   Data source cards\n--------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n.data-grid {\n  width: min(1050px, 92vw);\n  margin: 1.6rem auto 0 auto;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);\n  gap: 16px;\n}\n\n.data-card {\n  background: #FAF7F0;\n  border: 1px solid #E3D6B8;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 1.25rem 1.3rem;\n  text-align: left;\n  box-shadow: 0 5px 14px rgba(23, 77, 56, 0.06);\n}\n\n.data-card h3 {\n  margin-top: 0;\n  margin-bottom: 0.6rem;\n  color: #174D38;\n  font-size: 1.08rem;\n}\n\n.data-card p {\n  margin: 0;\n  line-height: 1.65;\n  color: #2B2B2B;\n}\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------\n   Workflow\n--------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n.workflow {\n  width: min(1080px, 94vw);\n  margin: 2rem auto 0 auto;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns:\n    1fr auto\n    1fr auto\n    1fr auto\n    1fr auto\n    1fr auto\n    1fr;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 10px;\n}\n\n.workflow-step {\n  background: #FAF7F0;\n  border: 1px solid #D9C89F;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 1rem 0.75rem;\n  min-height: 125px;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  justify-content: center;\n  box-shadow: 0 5px 14px rgba(23, 77, 56, 0.06);\n}\n\n.workflow-number {\n  font-size: 1.35rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: #C5A45A;\n  margin-bottom: 0.35rem;\n}\n\n.workflow-title {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: #174D38;\n  margin-bottom: 0.35rem;\n  font-size: 0.98rem;\n}\n\n.workflow-text {\n  font-size: 0.82rem;\n  line-height: 1.4;\n  color: #65766D;\n}\n\n.workflow-arrow {\n  font-size: 1.5rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: #C5A45A;\n}\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------\n   Priority weights\n--------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n.weight-grid {\n  width: min(900px, 90vw);\n  margin: 1.5rem auto 0 auto;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);\n  gap: 14px;\n}\n\n.weight-card {\n  background: #FAF7F0;\n  border: 1px solid #E3D6B8;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 1.15rem 0.85rem;\n  box-shadow: 0 5px 14px rgba(23, 77, 56, 0.06);\n}\n\n.weight-card .weight {\n  display: block;\n  font-size: 1.5rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: #174D38;\n  margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n}\n\n.weight-card .label {\n  display: block;\n  color: #2B2B2B;\n  line-height: 1.4;\n}\n\n/* Smaller supporting chart */\n\n.chart-wrap {\n  width: min(700px, 72vw);\n  margin: 1.8rem auto 0 auto;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n.chart-wrap img {\n  display: block;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: auto;\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(23, 77, 56, 0.07);\n}\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------\n   Notes\n--------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n.method-note {\n  max-width: 920px;\n  margin: 1.5rem auto 0 auto;\n  padding: 1rem 1.25rem;\n  background: #FAF7F0;\n  border-left: 4px solid #C5A45A;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  text-align: left;\n  color: #2B2B2B;\n  line-height: 1.7;\n}\n\n.limitations-grid {\n  width: min(1000px, 92vw);\n  margin: 1.5rem auto 0 auto;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);\n  gap: 14px;\n}\n\n.limitation-card {\n  background: #FAF7F0;\n  border: 1px solid #E3D6B8;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  padding: 1rem 1.1rem;\n  text-align: left;\n}\n\n.limitation-card strong {\n  color: #174D38;\n}\n\n.limitation-card p {\n  margin: 0;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------\n   Responsive\n--------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n@media (max-width: 1000px) {\n  .workflow {\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n  }\n\n  .workflow-arrow {\n    transform: rotate(90deg);\n  }\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 800px) {\n  .data-grid,\n  .limitations-grid {\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n  }\n\n  .weight-grid {\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);\n  }\n\n  .chart-wrap {\n    width: min(760px, 92vw);\n  }\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n  .weight-grid {\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n  }\n}\n</style>\n\n::: {.section-hero}\n\n# Methods & Data\n\nCooling Riyadh integrates satellite imagery, population estimates, building footprints, and spatial machine learning within a common **500 m analysis grid**.\n\nThe workflow preserves the spatial meaning of each dataset while allowing multiple urban indicators to be compared consistently across Riyadh.\n\n:::\n\n::: {.methods-section}\n\n## Data Sources\n\n<div class=\"data-grid\">\n\n<div class=\"data-card\">\n\n### Landsat Collection 2 Level-2\n\nUsed to derive **land surface temperature (LST)** and **NDVI**.\n\nSurface reflectance and surface temperature products were processed with cloud and cloud-shadow masking before the Riyadh mosaics were created.\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"data-card\">\n\n### WorldPop 2026\n\nUsed to estimate the spatial distribution of residents across Riyadh.\n\nPopulation values were summarized into the 500 m analysis grid to provide an estimated population for each cell.\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"data-card\">\n\n### Microsoft Building Footprints\n\nUsed to characterize the built environment.\n\nBuilding polygons were clipped to Riyadh and summarized using building count, total building footprint area, and building coverage percentage.\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"data-card\">\n\n### Riyadh Urban Boundary\n\nThe study area was defined using the Riyadh urban boundary extracted from the **Copernicus Global Human Settlement Layer Urban Centre Database**.\n\nThis boundary was used consistently for clipping, raster processing, and final visualization.\n\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n:::\n\n::: {.methods-section}\n\n## Analysis Workflow\n\n<div class=\"workflow\">\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">01</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">Prepare Data</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nClip, clean, and project the source datasets.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-arrow\">→</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">02</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">500 m Grid</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nCreate a common spatial unit across Riyadh.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-arrow\">→</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">03</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">Urban Indicators</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nCalculate LST, NDVI, population, and building metrics.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-arrow\">→</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">04</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">K-Means</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nIdentify recurring urban profiles using unsupervised machine learning.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-arrow\">→</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">05</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">Priority Score</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nCombine normalized indicators into a spatial screening score.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-arrow\">→</div>\n\n<div class=\"workflow-step\">\n<div class=\"workflow-number\">06</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-title\">AI-Assisted Interpretation</div>\n<div class=\"workflow-text\">\nCompare urban clusters with High and Very High priority areas.\n</div>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n:::\n\n::: {.methods-section}\n\n## Priority Score\n\nThe final greening priority score combines four normalized indicators.\n\n<div class=\"weight-grid\">\n\n<div class=\"weight-card\">\n<span class=\"weight\">35%</span>\n<span class=\"label\">Land Surface Temperature</span>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"weight-card\">\n<span class=\"weight\">30%</span>\n<span class=\"label\">Low Vegetation</span>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"weight-card\">\n<span class=\"weight\">25%</span>\n<span class=\"label\">Population Exposure</span>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"weight-card\">\n<span class=\"weight\">10%</span>\n<span class=\"label\">Building Coverage</span>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"chart-wrap\">\n\n![](assets/images/maps/Riyadh_Priority_Weights_Chart.png)\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"method-note\">\n\nThese weights are **analyst-defined** and reflect the project's research question. They are not statistically estimated model coefficients and should be interpreted as a transparent spatial screening framework.\n\n</div>\n\n:::\n\n::: {.methods-section}\n\n## Machine Learning & AI\n\nK-Means clustering was applied to four standardized variables:\n\n**Land Surface Temperature · NDVI · Population · Building Coverage**\n\nThe algorithm grouped spatial cells according to similarity without using predefined labels.\n\nThe resulting urban profiles were then compared with High and Very High greening-priority cells to create the **AI-assisted priority interpretation**.\n\n<div class=\"method-note\">\n\nThe machine-learning analysis supports interpretation of recurring urban conditions. It does **not** generate or replace the weighted greening priority score.\n\n</div>\n\n:::\n\n::: {.methods-section}\n\n## Important Limitations\n\n<div class=\"limitations-grid\">\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Land Surface Temperature</strong><br>\nLST represents satellite-derived surface temperature rather than direct air temperature.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Vegetation</strong><br>\nNDVI indicates vegetation presence but does not distinguish individual trees from grass, shrubs, or other vegetation.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Population</strong><br>\nWorldPop provides modeled population estimates rather than direct census counts for every grid cell.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Buildings</strong><br>\nBuilding footprints describe mapped building geometry but do not directly represent height, occupancy, material, or land use.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Priority Weights</strong><br>\nThe weighting scheme reflects the analytical objectives of this project and is not statistically optimized.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"limitation-card\">\n<p><strong>Intervention Readiness</strong><br>\nPriority areas identify locations for further assessment rather than direct planting recommendations.</p>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"method-note\">\n\nLocal land ownership, utilities, road geometry, water availability, existing projects, and planning constraints should be assessed before implementing any greening intervention.\n\n</div>\n\n:::"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":"auto","echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","css":["styles.css"],"toc":false,"include-before-body":[{"text":"<style>\n\n/* ========================